        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Heinrich August Marschner, Richard Wagner, Eduard Devrient, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Works: Moog Indigo, The Turkish March (Marcia alla turca)\n- Topics: German opera, Turkish-style classical music\n\nFacts:\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart wrote The Turkish March, also known as Marcia alla turca.\n- The Turkish March is a well-known classical march theme written in the Turkish style that was popular at the time.\n- Music written by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was covered on the album Moog Indigo.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was regarded as the most important composer of German opera between Eduard Devrient and Richard Wagner.",
